# AGENTS instructions

## Naming

Write **Dag** in prose. Keep `DAG` (all-caps) only for literal code tokens: `from airflow.sdk import DAG`, `dag_id`, `dag_processing/`, `airflow dags list`. Don't spell out "Directed Acyclic Graph" except for historical context.

## Environment Setup

- Install prek: `uv tool install prek` then `prek install`
- Install breeze shim (one-time): `scripts/tools/setup_breeze`
- **Never run pytest, python, or airflow directly on the host** — always use `breeze`
- Temporary scripts go in `dev/` (mounted as `/opt/airflow/dev/` inside Breeze)

## Commands

`<PROJECT>` = folder with `pyproject.toml` (e.g. `airflow-core`, `providers/amazon`). `<target_branch>` = merge target (usually `main`).

<!-- START generated-commands, please keep comment here to allow auto update -->
- **Run a single test:** `uv run --project <PROJECT> pytest path/to/test.py::TestClass::test_method -xvs`
- **Run a test file:** `uv run --project <PROJECT> pytest path/to/test.py -xvs`
- **Run all tests in package:** `uv run --project <PROJECT> pytest path/to/package -xvs`
- **If uv tests fail with missing system dependencies, run the tests with breeze**: `breeze run pytest <tests> -xvs`
- **Run a Python script:** `uv run --project <PROJECT> python dev/my_script.py`
- **Run core or provider tests suite in parallel:** `breeze testing <test_group> --run-in-parallel` (test groups: `core-tests`, `providers-tests`)
- **Run core or provider db tests suite in parallel:** `breeze testing <test_group> --run-db-tests-only --run-in-parallel` (test groups: `core-tests`, `providers-tests`)
- **Run core or provider non-db tests suite in parallel:** `breeze testing <test_group> --skip-db-tests --use-xdist` (test groups: `core-tests`, `providers-tests`)
- **Run single provider complete test suite:** `breeze testing providers-tests --test-type "Providers[PROVIDERS_LIST]"` (e.g., `Providers[google]` or `Providers[amazon]` or "Providers[amazon,google]")
- **Run Helm tests in parallel with xdist** `breeze testing helm-tests --use-xdist`
- **Run Helm tests with specific K8s version:** `breeze testing helm-tests --use-xdist --kubernetes-version 1.35.0`
- **Run specific Helm test type:** `breeze testing helm-tests --use-xdist --test-type <type>` (types: `airflow_aux`, `airflow_core`, `apiserver`, `dagprocessor`, `other`, `redis`, `security`, `statsd`, `webserver`)
- **Run other suites of tests** `breeze testing <test_group>` (test groups: `airflow-ctl-tests`, `docker-compose-tests`, `task-sdk-tests`)
- **Run scripts tests:** `uv run --project scripts pytest scripts/tests/ -xvs`
- **Run Airflow CLI:** `breeze run airflow dags list`
- **Type-check (non-providers):** `prek run mypy-<project> --all-files` (e.g. `mypy-airflow-core`, `mypy-task-sdk`, `mypy-shared-logging`; each `shared/<dist>` has its own `mypy-shared-<dist>` hook). Clear cache: `breeze down --cleanup-mypy-cache`.
- **Type-check (providers):** `breeze run mypy path/to/code`
- **Lint with ruff only:** `prek run ruff --from-ref <target_branch>`
- **Format with ruff only:** `prek run ruff-format --from-ref <target_branch>`
- **Run regular (fast) static checks:** `prek run --from-ref <target_branch> --stage pre-commit`
- **Run manual (slower) checks:** `prek run --from-ref <target_branch> --stage manual`
- **Build docs:** `breeze build-docs`
- **Determine which tests to run based on changed files:** `breeze selective-checks --commit-ref <commit_with_squashed_changes>`
<!-- END generated-commands, please keep comment here to allow auto update -->

SQLite is the default backend. Use `--backend postgres` or `--backend mysql` for DB integration tests. If Docker networking fails: `docker network prune`. If `uv.lock` conflicts, delete it and run `uv lock`.

## Repository Structure

UV workspace monorepo. Key paths:
- `airflow-core/src/airflow/` — scheduler, API, CLI, models, UI (React/Vite)
  - `models/` — SQLAlchemy models; `jobs/` — scheduler/triggerer runners
  - `api_fastapi/core_api/` — REST API v2; `api_fastapi/execution_api/` — task execution API
  - `dag_processing/` — Dag parsing; `cli/` — CLI; `ui/` — React/TypeScript
- `task-sdk/src/airflow/sdk/execution_time/` — task runner, supervisor
- `providers/` — 100+ provider packages, each with own `pyproject.toml`
- `airflow-ctl/` — management CLI; `chart/` — Helm chart
- `dev/` — dev utilities, breeze env, release tooling
- `scripts/` — CI, Docker, prek hooks (`ci/prek/`); tests at `scripts/tests/`
- `shared/` — small shared Python distributions (logging, config), symlinked into consumers

## Architecture Boundaries

1. Users author Dags with Task SDK (`airflow.sdk`).
2. Dag File Processor parses Dags in separate processes → serialized to metadata DB. Software guards enforce Execution API; do not protect against intentional bypass.
3. Scheduler reads serialized Dags — **never runs user code** — creates Dag runs/task instances.
4. Workers execute via Task SDK → Execution API only — **never access metadata DB directly**. Tasks get short-lived JWT tokens scoped to task instance ID.
5. API Server serves React UI and all client-DB interactions.
6. Triggerer evaluates deferred tasks in separate processes, same guards as DFP.
7. `shared/` libraries are symlinked to distributions (`airflow-core`, `task-sdk`, etc.).

## Security Model

Authoritative refs: [`airflow-core/docs/security/security_model.rst`](airflow-core/docs/security/security_model.rst) and [`jwt_token_authentication.rst`](airflow-core/docs/security/jwt_token_authentication.rst).

Distinguish when flagging concerns:
- **Actual vulnerabilities** — code violating the documented security model
- **Known limitations** — documented gaps (DFP/Triggerer DB access, shared Execution API); tracked for future improvement, not new findings
- **Deployment hardening** — belongs in deployment guidance, not code issues

## Coding Standards

- After writing/editing any Python file: `uv run ruff format <file>` then `uv run ruff check --fix <file>`
- No `assert` in production code
- `time.monotonic()` for durations, not `time.time()`
- In `airflow-core`: functions with `session` param must not call `session.commit()`; use keyword-only `session` params
- Imports at top of file (exceptions: circular imports, lazy loading for worker isolation, `TYPE_CHECKING`)
- Guard heavy type-only imports (e.g. `kubernetes.client`) with `TYPE_CHECKING` in multi-process paths
- **No new `raise AirflowException(...)` usages** — `check-no-new-airflow-exceptions` prek hook enforces this. Use `ValueError`, `TypeError`, `OSError`, or a dedicated class in `exceptions.py`. Narrowing existing ones is fine; adding new direct usages is not.
- Translate domain exceptions to `HTTPException` at FastAPI route boundaries (404 for not-found, 400 for invalid input)
- Bulk `DELETE`/`UPDATE` in scheduler loop must be batched with `LIMIT`, committed between batches. Follow pattern in `airflow-core/src/airflow/utils/db_cleanup.py`.
- Function names use action verbs: `get_`, `extract_`, `find_`, `compute_`, `build_`. Predicates: `is_`, `has_`.
- Apache License header on all new files (prek enforces)
- If changing `selective_checks.py`, update `dev/breeze/doc/ci/04_selective_checks.md` and tests in `dev/breeze/tests/test_selective_checks.py` in the same PR
- **Newsfragments**: only for `airflow-core/`, `chart/`, `dev/mypy/` — only for user-facing changes. **Never add for `providers/` or `airflow-ctl/`** (edit `providers/<provider>/docs/changelog.rst` or `airflow-ctl/RELEASE_NOTES.rst` directly). `task-sdk/` changes use `airflow-core/newsfragments/`. When in doubt, omit — a maintainer will ask.

## Testing Standards

- 100% coverage of PR changes — every changed behaviour needs a test that fails without the change; don't test pre-existing or stdlib/third-party logic
- pytest patterns, not `unittest.TestCase`
- `spec`/`autospec` when mocking; prefer `@mock.patch` decorator over context manager
- `conf_vars` (from `tests_common.test_utils.config`) for config overrides
- `time_machine` for time-dependent tests; no `datetime.now()`
- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` for multiple similar inputs
- `@pytest.mark.db_test` for DB-access tests
- Test fixtures: `devel-common/src/tests_common/pytest_plugin.py`
- Test location mirrors source: `airflow/cli/cli_parser.py` → `tests/cli/test_cli_parser.py`
- No `caplog` — check logic, not log output

## Output

Generated files (PR reviews, reports, scratch): put in `files/` (create if missing).

## Commits and PRs

- Commit messages: imperative mood, user-impact focused, plain prose — **no Conventional Commits prefixes** (`fix:`, `feat:`, `chore:`, …). `check-no-conventional-commit-message` prek hook rejects them. Area tags (`UI:`, `API:`, `Helm:`) are fine.
- Commit body: explain **why**, not what (the diff shows what).
- **Always run `prek install` before committing** (installs `commit-msg` hook).
- NEVER add `Co-Authored-By` with yourself as co-author.
- Before working on an issue, check for existing PRs: `gh pr list --search "<keywords>"`. Prefer building on existing work. **If fix is imminent, open the PR directly — not an issue first.**
- For workarounds/partial fixes: open a tracking issue first, reference it in the PR body, and add the full URL as a code comment at the workaround site.

### Git remotes

- `upstream` → `apache/airflow` (fetch only)
- `origin` → your fork (push PR branches here; never push to `upstream` or `main`)

Run `git remote -v` before any remote operation. If names don't match, propose renames and ask user to confirm before running.

### Creating PRs — pre-push checklist

1. `git diff main...HEAD` — verify every change is intentional, remove unrelated edits
2. Check `.github/instructions/code-review.instructions.md` against diff
3. `prek run --from-ref <target_branch> --stage pre-commit` — fix failures
4. `prek run --from-ref <target_branch> --stage manual` — fix failures
5. Run selective-checks to find relevant tests; run them in parallel
6. `git fetch upstream <target_branch> && git rebase upstream/<target_branch>`
7. `git push -u origin <branch-name>` then `gh pr create --web` — include `closes: #ISSUE`, check the generative AI disclosure box, add `Generated-by:` line per `contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions`.

### GitHub messages drafted by agents

End every agent-drafted message with: `---\nDrafted-by: <Agent> (no human review)` or `---\nDrafted-by: <Agent>; reviewed by @<handle>`. Do NOT tag individuals unless explicitly instructed or replying to active participants.

## apache-magpie

Repo uses [`apache/magpie`](https://github.com/apache/magpie) framework. On fresh clone, run `/magpie-setup` to populate `.apache-magpie/` snapshot. Modifications go in `.apache-magpie-overrides/` — never edit the snapshot. Use `magpie-pr-management-code-review` skill for PR reviews (posts inline comments per file:line).

## Boundaries

- **Ask first:** large cross-package refactors, new broad-impact dependencies, destructive data/migration changes
- **Never:** commit secrets/credentials, hand-edit generated files, use destructive git ops unless explicitly requested

